<h2>Construction and Real Estate Development: Specialized Sector Frameworks</h2>
<p>Construction and real estate businesses face unique licensing requirements reflecting project complexity, safety obligations, and financial scale. The sector\'s regulatory framework distinguishes between contractors, developers, real estate brokers, and property management companies.</p>
<h3>Contractor Classification and Licensing</h3>
<p>The <strong>Ministry of Municipal and Rural Affairs and Housing</strong> operates contractor classification systems that determine eligible project types. Contractors receive grades from Grade Five (smallest projects) to Grade One (mega-projects) based on technical capacity, financial strength, and project history.</p>
