<h3>Document Preparation and Authentication Costs</h3>
<p>Professional documentation services constitute a significant cost component. Certified translations average SAR 150 to SAR 300 per page depending on document complexity and language pair. Arabic-to-English translations for legal documents often cost more due to specialized terminology requirements.</p>
<p>Embassy authentication and legalization fees vary by nationality. Investors from countries with Saudi diplomatic missions pay SAR 300 to SAR 800 per document. Nationals from countries without Saudi representation must use third-party authentication services costing SAR 1,000 to SAR 2,000 per document.</p>
<p>Legal review and <strong>articles of association</strong> drafting require specialized expertise. Experienced corporate lawyers charge SAR 8,000 to SAR 25,000 for comprehensive drafting, review, and filing services. Inadequate articles of association create operational restrictions and governance problems that prove costly to rectify later.</p>
<h3>Professional Service Fees</h3>
<p>Full-service business formation consultancies like Motaded offer comprehensive packages covering every registration step. Service packages typically range from SAR 20,000 to SAR 60,000 depending on complexity, urgency, and included services. These packages encompass:</p>
