<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>Q: Can I reserve multiple names simultaneously for different business concepts?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Yes, you can submit separate reservation applications for different business entities. Each application requires independent payment of the 200 SAR fee and generates distinct reservation certificates. However, names must reflect genuinely different business activities and cannot be placeholder reservations without active formation intent.</p>
<h3>Q: What happens if someone registers my reserved name after my sixty-day expiration?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Once your reservation expires without CR completion, the name returns to the available pool. Other applicants can legitimately reserve and register it. No priority rights exist for previous reservation holders. To prevent this, submit your Commercial Registration application before expiration or request a paid extension.</p>
<h3>Q: Do I need a separate name reservation for branch offices of my existing company?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> No, branch registrations use your parent company\'s approved business name with geographic designation. For example, "ABC Trading Company LLC - Jeddah Branch." The original name reservation covers all branches registered under the same CR entity. However, subsidiaries structured as separate legal entities require independent name reservations.</p>
<h3>Q: Can I modify my reserved name spelling after certificate issuance but before CR registration?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Minor corrections for typographical errors can be requested through Markaz support with documentation explaining the mistake. Substantive name changes require abandoning your current reservation and submitting a new application with full fee payment. Modifications that alter the name\'s meaning or distinctiveness are treated as new reservations.</p>
