<h3>Anti-Money Laundering Cooperation</h3>
<p>Banks must report suspicious transactions to the <strong>Saudi Financial Intelligence Unit</strong> under anti-money laundering regulations. Refusing to cooperate with bank inquiries or providing false information constitutes serious violations that result in account termination and regulatory referrals. Always respond honestly and promptly to compliance questions.</p>
<p>Implement internal controls demonstrating your commitment to regulatory compliance. Document your customer verification procedures, transaction approval processes, and record-keeping systems. These controls protect your business and satisfy bank due diligence requirements during periodic account reviews.</p>
