<h2>Understanding VAT Rates and Categories in Saudi Arabia</h2>
<p>Saudi Arabia applies different VAT rates depending on the goods or services supplied. Understanding which rate applies to your business activities ensures accurate invoicing and compliance. Incorrect rate application is a common audit finding that results in penalties and back-tax assessments.</p>
<p>The standard VAT rate is 15 percent, applied to most goods and services. This includes retail sales, hospitality, professional services, and imported goods. If your business supplies standard-rated items, you charge 15 percent VAT on every invoice and remit the collected amount to ZATCA after deducting eligible input VAT.</p>
<p>Zero-rated supplies carry a 0 percent VAT rate but remain taxable supplies. This category includes exports of goods and services outside the Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC), international transportation, and certain medical supplies. Businesses making zero-rated supplies can reclaim input VAT on related expenses, making this category advantageous for exporters.</p>
