      'body' => '<h1>How to Get a Company Stamp (Seal) in Saudi Arabia</h1>
<p>A <strong>company stamp</strong> or <strong>seal</strong> is a mandatory legal requirement for businesses operating in Saudi Arabia. Every official document—from contracts and bank applications to government filings—requires a stamped signature for validation. Understanding the company stamp seal how to get ksa process ensures your business remains compliant and operational from day one. This guide walks you through where to order your stamp, what information it must contain, and how to avoid common mistakes that delay business activities.</p>
<h2>Why Your Business Needs an Official Company Stamp</h2>
<p>The company stamp serves as your business\'s physical signature on all formal documentation. Without it, you cannot execute contracts, open corporate bank accounts, or submit applications to government entities like <strong>ZATCA</strong> or the <strong>Ministry of Commerce</strong>.</p>
<p>Saudi regulations require the stamp to authenticate every transaction your business conducts. Banks will refuse account opening requests without stamped application forms. Government portals reject submissions lacking proper stamp authentication.</p>
<p><strong>Motaded</strong> handles stamp procurement as part of comprehensive company formation services, ensuring your seal meets all regulatory specifications before you approach banks or government offices. Visit motaded.com.sa to streamline this essential step.</p>
<h3>Legal Documents Requiring Company Stamps</h3>
<p>The following documents must carry your company stamp for legal validity:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Commercial Registration</strong> certificate applications and renewals</li>
<li>Bank account opening forms and signature cards</li>
<li>Employment contracts and <strong>Nitaqat Saudization</strong> compliance documents</li>
<li>Supplier agreements and procurement bids for <strong>Etimad platform</strong> registration</li>
<li>Tax registration forms submitted to ZATCA</li>
<li>Real estate lease agreements for office spaces</li>
<li>Authorization letters for employee transactions</li>
</ul>
<h2>What Information Must Appear on Your Company Stamp</h2>
<p>Saudi regulations specify exact information your company stamp must display. Missing or incorrect details render the stamp legally invalid and unusable for official purposes.</p>
<p>Your stamp must include your complete <strong>Commercial Registration</strong> name exactly as printed on your CR certificate. Any deviation—even minor spelling differences—creates legal complications during document verification.</p>
<h3>Mandatory Stamp Elements</h3>
<p>Every company stamp in Saudi Arabia must contain these elements:</p>
<ol>
<li>Full legal company name in English</li>
<li><strong>Commercial Registration</strong> number (CR number)</li>
<li>Company type designation: <strong>LLC</strong>, sole establishment, branch, or representative office</li>
<li>City of registration (Riyadh, Jeddah, Dammam, etc.)</li>
</ol>
<p>The stamp shape is typically circular or rectangular, measuring 40-50mm in diameter. Rectangular stamps usually measure 60mm x 30mm. Both formats comply with regulatory standards.</p>

<h3>Optional Stamp Information</h3>
<p>Some businesses add supplementary details for enhanced clarity:</p>
<ul>
<li>Registration date for operational reference</li>
<li>Primary business activity code from CR certificate</li>
<li>Contact telephone number for verification purposes</li>
<li>Company logo integration for brand consistency</li>
</ul>
<p>Including these elements remains optional. They do not affect legal validity but may streamline verification processes with certain government departments.</p>
<h2>Step-by-Step Process to Obtain Your Company Stamp</h2>
<p>Acquiring a company stamp involves selecting a licensed vendor and providing verified documentation. The entire process typically completes within 24-48 hours after document submission.</p>
<h3>Step 1: Complete Your Commercial Registration</h3>
<p>You cannot order a company stamp until you possess a valid <strong>Commercial Registration</strong> certificate. The CR document contains the exact legal name and registration number required for stamp production.</p>
<p>Foreign investors establishing an <strong>LLC</strong> or obtaining a <strong>MISA investment license</strong> must wait for CR issuance before approaching stamp vendors. Attempting to order stamps prematurely results in rejected orders.</p>
<p>Businesses following the <strong>business setup process in Saudi Arabia</strong> should coordinate stamp ordering immediately after receiving their CR certificate to avoid operational delays.
<h3>Step 2: Locate Licensed Stamp Vendors</h3>
<p>Licensed stamp manufacturers operate in commercial districts across major Saudi cities. These vendors specialize in producing official company seals that meet regulatory specifications.</p>
<p>In Riyadh, stamp shops concentrate near the Chamber of Commerce and <strong>Ministry of Commerce</strong> offices. Jeddah vendors cluster around the business districts of Al Khalidiyah and Al Rawdah.</p>
<p>You may also commission stamps through online platforms that deliver nationwide. These services require digital copies of your CR certificate and complete production within 2-3 business days.</p>
<h3>Step 3: Provide Required Documentation</h3>
<p>Stamp vendors need specific documents to verify your business legitimacy and ensure accurate information:</p>
<ul>
<li>Original <strong>Commercial Registration</strong> certificate or certified copy</li>
<li>National ID or <strong>Iqama</strong> of the company representative</li>
<li>Authorization letter if a third party collects the stamp</li>
</ul>
<p>Vendors photograph or scan these documents for their records. This verification protects against fraudulent stamp production and ensures compliance with security regulations.</p>
<p>Motaded can arrange stamp production through verified vendors during your company formation journey, coordinating timing with bank account opening requirements—motaded.com.sa.</p>
<h3>Step 4: Review Stamp Proof and Approve Production</h3>
<p>Professional vendors provide a digital proof showing your stamp design before production begins. Review this proof carefully for accuracy in name spelling, CR number, and company type designation.</p>
<p>Corrections at the proof stage cost nothing. Changes after production require complete remake and additional fees. Compare the proof against your original CR certificate word-by-word.</p>
<p>Most stamp shops complete production within 24 hours of proof approval. Rush services deliver finished stamps in 4-6 hours for additional fees.</p>
<h3>Step 5: Collect Your Stamp and Test Impression</h3>
<p>Upon collection, test your stamp impression on plain paper before leaving the vendor\'s premises. Verify that all text appears clearly and completely with proper ink transfer.</p>
<p>Request replacement immediately if the impression shows smudging, incomplete letters, or misaligned text. Quality vendors provide free replacement for production defects within the first week.</p>
<p>Store your company stamp securely in a locked drawer or safe. Unauthorized stamp use exposes your business to contract fraud and financial liability.</p>
<h2>Company Stamp Seal How to Get KSA: Cost and Timeframe</h2>
<p>Standard company stamps cost between <strong>150-300 SAR</strong> depending on size, material quality, and production speed. Basic rubber stamps with plastic handles represent the lower price range.</p>
<p>Self-inking stamps—which require no separate ink pad—typically cost <strong>250-400 SAR</strong>. These models suit high-volume document processing and provide cleaner, more consistent impressions.</p>
<p>Premium metal stamps with engraved designs range from <strong>500-800 SAR</strong>. While more expensive, metal stamps last significantly longer than rubber alternatives and project enhanced professionalism.</p>
