<p><strong>A:</strong> Most businesses function effectively with two stamps—one for daily operations and a backup for security purposes. Larger organizations or multi-location businesses may require additional stamps for different departments or branch offices. Each stamp must clearly identify its specific authorized use scope.</p>
<h3>Q: What should I do if my company stamp gets lost or stolen?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Immediately file a police report documenting the loss and obtain an official report copy. Notify all banks and government offices where you conduct business about the lost stamp. Commission a replacement stamp with identical specifications. Maintain the police report permanently as evidence of proper security protocols.</p>
<h3>Q: Do foreign branch offices need separate stamps from headquarters?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Yes, Saudi branches of foreign companies require distinct stamps showing their branch designation and Saudi Commercial Registration details. These stamps differ from parent company seals used in home countries. Branch stamps must display Saudi CR numbers and comply with local regulatory specifications completely.</p>
