      'body' => '<h1>Commercial Registration Fees in Saudi Arabia: What to Expect</h1>
<p>Understanding <strong>commercial registration fees saudi arabia 2026</strong> is essential for any entrepreneur or investor planning to establish a business in the Kingdom. The <strong>Commercial Registration (CR)</strong> process involves multiple fee components managed by the <strong>Ministry of Commerce (MoC)</strong> and other regulatory bodies. From name reservation to annual renewals, each step carries specific costs that directly impact your startup budget. This comprehensive guide breaks down every fee you\'ll encounter during the registration process, helping you plan accurately and avoid unexpected expenses during your business formation journey.</p>
<h2>Core Commercial Registration Fee Structure</h2>
<p>The Ministry of Commerce governs all commercial registration activities in Saudi Arabia. The core CR fee varies based on your business structure, activity classification, and registration location. <strong>Limited Liability Companies (LLCs)</strong> face different fee schedules compared to branch offices or sole establishments.</p>
<p>The basic CR issuance fee starts at SAR 200 for simple commercial activities. However, this baseline figure doesn\'t reflect the complete cost structure. Complex business activities requiring multiple licenses or special approvals can push initial registration fees significantly higher.</p>
<h3>Primary Registration Fee Components</h3>
<p>When calculating your total registration expense, consider these mandatory elements:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Initial CR issuance</strong>: SAR 200 to SAR 800 depending on business type</li>
<li><strong>Name reservation fee</strong>: SAR 200 per application</li>
<li><strong>Ministry processing charges</strong>: SAR 100 to SAR 500 based on entity structure</li>
<li><strong>Certificate authentication</strong>: SAR 50 per document copy</li>
</ul>

<h3>Business Structure Impact on Fees</h3>
<p>Your chosen legal structure directly affects registration costs. <strong>LLCs</strong> typically incur higher fees due to their complex ownership requirements and articles of association filing. Branch offices pay different rates since they represent foreign parent companies rather than independent Saudi entities.</p>
<p>Single-owner establishments generally face the lowest registration fees. However, this apparent cost saving often proves misleading when you factor in liability exposure and operational limitations that come with simpler structures.</p>
<h2>Name Reservation and Trademark Costs</h2>
<p>Before obtaining your CR, you must secure a business name through the <strong>Eonot system</strong>. The name reservation process operates separately from the main registration, carrying its own fee structure. Many founders underestimate this preliminary cost when building their initial budgets.</p>
<p>The standard name reservation fee is SAR 200 per submission. If your first choice is rejected or already taken, each subsequent application costs another SAR 200. Some entrepreneurs spend SAR 600 to SAR 1,000 on multiple name attempts before securing approval.</p>
<h3>Name Reservation Fee Breakdown</h3>
