<h2>Professional Service Retainers That Add Up Quickly</h2>
<p>Beyond the one-time <strong>business setup consultant fees saudi arabia</strong>, you need ongoing professional services from day one. A local <strong>chartered accountant</strong> retainer for monthly bookkeeping and tax compliance starts at SAR 2,000 to SAR 4,000 monthly. Annual audits add another SAR 8,000 to SAR 20,000 depending on company size.</p>
<p><strong>Legal counsel</strong> retainers cost SAR 3,000 to SAR 8,000 monthly for contract review, employment agreements, and regulatory compliance. Most international firms opening in Saudi Arabia underestimate these recurring professional fees, assuming they only pay for initial setup.</p>
<p><strong>ZATCA registration</strong> for VAT requires a tax agent or accountant to manage quarterly filings. Even if your revenue sits below the mandatory registration threshold, voluntary registration brings compliance costs. Zakat and corporate tax filings add SAR 5,000 to SAR 15,000 annually in professional fees.</p>
<h3>The Real Cost of Articles of Association Drafting</h3>
<p>Your company\'s <strong>articles of association saudi arabia</strong> must be drafted in Arabic by a licensed attorney and notarized before submission. Standard templates exist, but customization for foreign ownership structures, management clauses, and capital requirements needs legal expertise. Professional AoA drafting costs SAR 3,000 to SAR 8,000.</p>
<p>If your ownership structure includes multiple foreign shareholders or complex governance arrangements, drafting fees rise to SAR 10,000 to SAR 20,000. Amendments after initial submission cost SAR 2,000 to SAR 5,000 each.</p>
<p><strong>Professional service costs year one:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Accounting retainer: SAR 24,000–48,000 annually</li>
<li>Legal counsel retainer: SAR 36,000–96,000 annually</li>
<li>Annual audit: SAR 8,000–20,000</li>
<li>Articles of Association drafting: SAR 3,000–20,000</li>
<li>Tax filing support: SAR 5,000–15,000 annually</li>
<li>Total: SAR 76,000–199,000</li>
</ul>

<h2>Banking Costs and Minimum Balance Requirements</h2>
<p>Opening a corporate bank account in Saudi Arabia requires the completed <strong>Commercial Registration</strong>, but banks impose costs that surprise new business owners. Most banks charge SAR 1,000 to SAR 3,000 for account opening and setup. Monthly maintenance fees range from SAR 200 to SAR 800 depending on account type and transaction volume.</p>
<p><strong>Minimum balance requirements</strong> represent the biggest hidden cost. Banks typically require SAR 50,000 to SAR 200,000 maintained continuously in the account. Dropping below this threshold triggers penalty fees of SAR 500 to SAR 1,500 monthly. This working capital sits locked in your account, unavailable for operations.</p>
<p>International wire transfer fees cost SAR 100 to SAR 300 per transaction. Currency conversion charges add another one to three percent on every foreign payment. If you plan regular international transactions, these fees compound quickly.</p>
<h3>Capital Deposit Requirements for LLC Formation</h3>
<p><strong>LLC formation saudi arabia</strong> requires depositing the minimum share capital before Commercial Registration approval. For most business activities, this minimum sits at SAR 1,000, but specific industries require substantially more. Contracting companies need SAR 500,000, while some professional services require SAR 100,000.</p>
<p>This capital must remain deposited until after CR issuance. Banks charge SAR 500 to SAR 1,500 for capital verification letters required during registration. If you need to increase capital later, amendment fees reach SAR 3,000 to SAR 8,000.</p>
