<p>Foreign investors establishing <strong>LLC formations in Saudi Arabia</strong> benefit from 100% ownership across most sectors. The capital\'s regulatory environment facilitates technology, consulting, healthcare, and professional services entities without local partnership requirements.</p>
<h3>Legal Entity Formation Expenses</h3>
<p>Company registration KSA processes require <strong>Commercial Registration (CR)</strong> through the Ministry of Commerce, <strong>articles of association</strong> notarization, and capital deposit verification. Riyadh-specific costs include notary fees that slightly exceed other cities due to demand.</p>
<p><strong>Limited Liability Company (LLC)</strong> formation represents the most common structure. Minimum capital requirements vary by sector: SAR 1 for most activities, SAR 5 million for insurance, SAR 200,000 for manpower recruitment. Real estate and contracting activities carry sector-specific minimums.</p>

