<h2>Municipal Business License Fees by Region</h2>
<p>Every city and municipality charges location-specific business license fees separate from your CR. These permits authorize physical operations at your registered address. Fee schedules vary between Riyadh, Jeddah, Dammam, and other cities based on local regulations and zoning classifications.</p>
<p>Riyadh municipality charges SAR 500 to SAR 2,000 annually depending on business premises size and location zone. Commercial zones carry higher fees than industrial areas. Retail operations in premium districts face maximum fee brackets.
<h3>Location Permit and Occupancy Fees</h3>
<p>Beyond the municipal business license, you need Civil Defense approval for your premises. Civil Defense inspections cost SAR 300 to SAR 600 based on property classification and safety equipment requirements. Food service establishments and manufacturing facilities undergo enhanced inspections with fees reaching SAR 1,200.</p>
<p>Occupancy certificates from municipal authorities cost an additional SAR 400. Lease contract registration through the municipal portal carries SAR 200 filing fees.
<h2>Chamber of Commerce Membership Fees</h2>
<p>Chamber of Commerce membership becomes mandatory once you receive your CR. Annual membership fees depend on business size and declared capital. First-year registration includes a one-time enrollment charge plus annual dues.</p>
<p>Small businesses with capital under SAR 100,000 pay SAR 800 annual membership. Medium enterprises with capital between SAR 100,000 and SAR 5,000,000 face SAR 1,500 yearly fees. Large corporations exceeding SAR 5,000,000 capital pay SAR 3,000 or more based on specific brackets.</p>
<h3>Certificate Issuance and Authentication Services</h3>
<p>Chambers issue various business certificates required for banking, contracting, and government tenders. Certificate of Origin documents cost SAR 50 per certificate. Membership verification letters for bank account opening run SAR 100 each. Commercial invoice authentication ranges from SAR 30 to SAR 80 depending on document complexity.</p>

<h2>ZATCA Tax Registration and VAT Fees</h2>
<p><strong>ZATCA</strong> registration for Value Added Tax becomes mandatory for businesses projecting annual revenue above SAR 375,000. The registration itself carries no direct government fee, but non-compliance penalties start at SAR 10,000. E-invoicing system integration through approved providers costs SAR 800 to SAR 2,000 annually depending on transaction volume.</p>
<p>Tax Group Number applications for corporate structures cost nothing officially but require comprehensive documentation preparation. ZATCA certification for tax agents and representatives demands specialized qualifications beyond standard registration requirements.</p>
<h3>Zakat and Income Tax Filing Obligations</h3>
<p>Saudi nationals pay Zakat while foreign entities pay corporate income tax, but registration obligations apply universally. Annual tax return filing through the ZATCA portal carries no submission fee. However, late filing penalties reach SAR 1,000 minimum plus 2.5 percent monthly charges on unpaid amounts.</p>
<h2>Labour Office Registration and Nitaqat Fees</h2>
<p>The Ministry of Human Resources requires employer registration before hiring staff. Initial establishment registration costs SAR 400 through the Qiwa platform. Work permit applications cost SAR 2,000 per foreign employee annually plus SAR 400 work permit issuance fees.</p>
<p><strong>Nitaqat</strong> Saudization compliance monitoring carries no direct registration fee but impacts your operational costs significantly. Premium entities in excellent Nitaqat status access subsidies reducing per-employee fees by up to SAR 500 monthly through government incentive programs.</p>
<h3>Work Permit and Residency Fees</h3>
<p>Each foreign employee requires residence permits costing SAR 650 annually per dependent family member. Permit extensions run SAR 650 per year. Multiple entry exit re-entry visas cost SAR 200 for three months or SAR 500 for six-month validity.</p>

