<p><strong>Step 2</strong>: Review the fee calculation displayed in your dashboard. Verify that capital amounts, branch counts, and activity classifications match your current business structure. Discrepancies require correction before payment.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3</strong>: Generate the SADAD payment invoice through the system. This creates a unique billing reference number linked to your CR number and valid for 30 days.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4</strong>: Complete payment through any bank channel—online banking, ATM, or branch counter. Most banks process Chamber payments instantly through SADAD codes.</p>
<p><strong>Step 5</strong>: Return to Eonot to confirm payment registration. The system updates your membership status within 24 hours. Download the updated membership certificate for your records.</p>
<p><strong>Step 6</strong>: Proceed with CR renewal through the same portal. Active Chamber membership is verified automatically before the Ministry issues your renewed Commercial Registration.</p>
