<p><strong>Jeddah</strong> provides strong access to western region markets and benefits from its business-friendly environment and growing technology community. The city\'s coastal location and international character attract foreign tech talent more readily than inland locations.</p>
<p>Technology companies should explore opportunities in emerging tech zones and smart city developments that offer incentives, reduced establishment costs, or simplified regulatory procedures. Some locations provide free zone benefits including tax advantages and enhanced foreign ownership flexibility.
<h3>Office Space and Infrastructure Requirements</h3>
<p>MISA requires proof of physical office space before final license issuance. Technology companies need office addresses for Commercial Registration, even if operations occur primarily in cloud environments or through remote work arrangements.</p>
<p>Coworking spaces, technology incubators, and serviced offices satisfy MISA\'s physical presence requirements while minimizing initial real estate commitments. Some technology activities require specific infrastructure like server rooms, testing facilities, or client demonstration spaces that influence location and facility selection.</p>

