<p>The streamlined timeline resulted from pre-planned document preparation and professional handling of parallel registrations. Technology sector prioritization and absence of physical facility requirements contributed to efficiency.</p>
<h3>Trading Company Scenario</h3>
<p>An import-export trading company for consumer electronics with warehouse facilities required <strong>54 days</strong> total:</p>
<ul>
<li>Document preparation including financial guarantees: 14 days</li>
<li>MISA investment license review: 8 days</li>
<li>Trade name approval and CR: 9 days</li>
<li>Warehouse municipality inspection and approval: 15 days</li>
<li>Customs registration and SABER system setup: 8 days</li>
</ul>
<p>The physical facility inspection created the longest single delay, demonstrating how operational model choices directly impact timelines. Earlier warehouse identification would have enabled parallel municipality processing.</p>
<h3>Consulting Firm Scenario</h3>
<p>A management consulting firm established by two foreign partners as an LLC achieved operational status in <strong>38 days</strong>:</p>
