<p><strong>General Organization for Social Insurance (GOSI):</strong> Branches employing staff in Saudi Arabia must register with GOSI and make monthly contributions. Social insurance requirements apply to both Saudi and expatriate employees, though contribution rates differ.</p>
<p><strong>Labor Office Registration:</strong> The Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development requires establishment file creation. This registration enables visa allocation, work permit processing, and <strong>Nitaqat</strong> Saudization program compliance. Motaded assists with initial labor office setup and ongoing compliance monitoring.</p>
<h3>Nitaqat Saudization Requirements for Branches</h3>
<p>The Nitaqat program mandates minimum Saudi employment percentages varying by company size and sector. Branch offices fall under the same requirements as independent entities for Saudization purposes. Failure to meet required percentages results in penalties including visa quota restrictions.</p>
<p>Small branches with fewer than ten employees face lower percentage requirements, but the Ministry regularly adjusts thresholds. Maintaining compliant Saudization levels requires proactive workforce planning. Companies in specialized sectors may qualify for exemptions or reduced targets based on skill availability.</p>
<p>Motaded\'s HR compliance team monitors Nitaqat requirement changes and implements strategies to maintain your branch in favorable classification bands.
