<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>Q: Can I cancel my CR if I have outstanding tax obligations?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> No. <strong>ZATCA</strong> must issue final tax clearances before the <strong>Ministry of Commerce</strong> approves <strong>CR</strong> cancellation applications. You must settle all tax liabilities, file final returns, and obtain formal clearance certificates documenting zero balances across VAT, Zakat, corporate income tax, and withholding tax categories before proceeding with dissolution.</p>
<h3>Q: What happens to my employees during CR cancellation?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> You must terminate all employment contracts following proper labor law procedures before <strong>CR</strong> cancellation approval. Employees receive end-of-service benefits, notice period payments, unused leave compensation, and proper visa cancellations. Foreign workers require exit documentation and repatriation arrangements. Labor authority clearances confirming proper termination procedures are mandatory for dissolution approval.</p>
<h3>Q: How long must I retain business records after CR cancellation?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Financial statements require ten-year retention. Tax documents must remain accessible for five years after final return filing. Employee records need five-year retention from termination dates. Commercial contracts should be maintained for their term plus five years. <strong>CR</strong> and license documents warrant permanent retention for potential future reference or regulatory inquiries.</p>
<h3>Q: Can foreign investors restart business after CR cancellation?</h3>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Yes. Previous <strong>CR</strong> cancellation does not prevent future business establishment in Saudi Arabia. However, you must complete entirely new registration procedures including fresh <strong>MISA investment license</strong> applications, entity formation, and <strong>CR</strong> issuance. Your cancelled <strong>CR</strong> number and previous business name may not be available for reuse.</p>
