<h2>CR Application Submission Through Ministry of Commerce Platforms</h2>
<p>After securing your MISA license, depositing required capital, and finalizing constitutional documents, you proceed to actual CR application submission. The <strong>Ministry of Commerce</strong> processes all CR applications through digital platforms requiring authenticated access and document uploads in specified formats.</p>
<p>Your application links your MISA license number, attaches banking capital certificates, and uploads Arabic-language Articles of Association. The system validates license-activity consistency, verifies capital adequacy against activity requirements, and performs automated compliance checks before forwarding applications for human review.</p>
<p>Processing timelines for foreign-owned company CR applications extend beyond domestic entity processing. Expect four to eight weeks from complete application submission to CR certificate issuance. Incomplete applications or document deficiencies trigger rejection notices requiring resubmission, extending timelines by additional weeks.</p>
<h3>Step-by-Step CR Application Process</h3>
<p><strong>Step 1: Access Ministry of Commerce Portal</strong>
Register on the Ministry\'s business portal using your MISA license reference. Create authenticated login credentials with authorized manager information. Verify email and mobile contact details for application status communications.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Initiate CR Application Module</strong>
Select foreign-owned entity classification matching your MISA license type. Enter proposed commercial name in Arabic and verify availability against existing registrations. Reserve approved name for your application processing period.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Upload Required Documentation</strong>
Attach MISA investment license PDF, bank capital certificate, notarized Articles of Association, and manager identification documents. Ensure all uploads meet technical specifications for file size, format, and language requirements.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Specify Business Activities</strong>
Enter ISIC codes matching activities approved in your MISA license. Add secondary activities within permitted scope. Verify activity descriptions match Articles of Association declarations exactly.</p>
<p><strong>Step 5: Submit Application and Pay Fees</strong>
Review complete application for accuracy before final submission. Pay applicable CR registration fees through integrated payment gateway. Retain payment confirmation reference for tracking purposes.</p>
<p><strong>Step 6: Monitor Application Status</strong>
Track application progress through portal status updates. Respond promptly to any Ministry requests for clarification or additional documentation. Expect preliminary review completion within two weeks of submission.</p>
